The distance traveled by the tip of the hour hand is $2\cdot 6\cdot10 \pi=120\pi$ inches, while that of the tip of the minute hand is $2\cdot 8 \cdot 15\pi = 240\pi$ inches.  Their ratio, expressed in terms of a common fraction is $\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.

OR

The hour hand covers 1/4 of the total distance between consecutive positions of the minute hand while the minute hand covers 3/4 of the total distance between consecutive positions of the hour hand.  Hence, the ratio of their traveled distances must be $1/4$ to $3/4$, or in simpler terms, $\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}.$ </think> <answer> \frac{1}{2} </answer>

