\end{align*}
We also know that the sum of all three numbers $x$, $y$, and $z$ is $165$. We substitute for $z$ and $y$ as stated above, and solve for $n$:
\begin{align*}x+y+z&=165 \\x+y+n-9&=165 \\x+y+n&=174
\\\Rightarrow\qquad 7x+n&=174\\ n&=174-7x\\5-7&=-7x+n\\5&=-6x+n+9\\5&=9+9\\ 5\times 7&=n+9\times 7 \\ 56&=n \\ n+9&=z+9 \\ n&=z\\
\end{align*}
Now that we know that $n=z$, then we substitute $z$ for $n$ to find that the smallest number equals the third number. We also know that $n=56$, so now we can back substitute that:
\begin{align*}
7\times x& = 56+9\\ \Rightarrow\qquad x& = 65/7\\ \Rightarrow\qquad x& = 9.2857\\ \end{align*}
We know again that $y=z+9$ and $z = n = 56$, so now we can find another number. \begin{align*}
y& = z + 9 \\ y& = 56 + 9 \\ y& = 65 \\ n& = 56\end{align*}
Now that we know the value of $z$, we can solve for $y$, then solve for $x$. $x+y+z=165$ implying $9.2857+y+56=165$ and adding $9$ to both sides gives $y+56+9.2857=\boxed{165+9}$. </think> <answer> 165+9 </answer>

